  "ingredients": [
    "4 large egg yolk",
    "1/4 cup erythritol (powdered)",
    "6 tablespoon water",
    "1 1/2 cup heavy whipping cream",
    "1/4 teaspoon liquid stevia",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt",
    "1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1 teaspoon maple extract",
    "1 tablespoon low-carb maple syrup"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 300F. Begin by separating out the egg yolks and set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1842.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a spice grinder to powder the erythritol. Be careful when taking the lid off, as the powder could float into the air. Letting the powder settle a few moments before removing the lid helps with this.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1844.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the powdered erythritol with water in a small saucepan.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1848.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a larger saucepan, combine the heavy cream, liquid stevia, salt, vanilla extract, and maple extract.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1854.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring both of the mixtures to a rolling boil. Once the cream reaches a boil, stir vigorously and turn the heat down to low. Keep stirring this occasionally as you work with the other mixture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1858.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the water and erythritol have been boiling for a minute, add in the Low-Carb Maple Syrup.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1868.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk the egg yolks well, until they take on a paler color.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1873.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Continue boiling the water and erythritol mixture until it has reduced to form a thin syrup.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1875.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour the water and erythritol mixture into the heavy cream and stir to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1881.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slowly add the cream mixture to the egg yolks, pouring in about one-quarter of the mixture at a time. You want to temper the egg yolks, so make sure not to add too much at once.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1882.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour the mixture into ramekins, about half full.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1887.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fill a baking sheet two-thirds of the way full with water. Place the ramekins in the water and bake for 40 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-11",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1891.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the oven and let cool for 10–15 minutes. You can refrigerate these if you prefer more of a light custard or pudding texture. You can also eat them warm for a velvety soft, smooth texture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-12",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/IMG_1892.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Who are we kidding? Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/caramel-pots-de-creme/#wprm-recipe-51089-step-0-13",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
